{"raw": {"https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Grounds-Worker--Accepting-Applications-_R0001298": {"title": "Grounds Worker (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Grounds Worker (Accepting Applications) Job Description: Perform all duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: GROUNDS Must be knowledgeable of all basic aspects of general landscaping, including planting, pruning, shearing, mulching, mowing, trimming, blowing, leaf removal, snow removal, watering, policing grounds, trash removal, paver or wall installations, grading and turf renovation, sod installation, fertilizer and pesticide application, weeding, tree removal, and basic computer/record keeping. May be asked to assist any other department within the campus community and will be required to perform any other duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Must be willing and able to work independently without supervision. Snow removal duties will be necessary seasonally. A uniform, issued by MSMU will be required. May be asked to assist any other department within the campus community and will be required to perform any other duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Must be willing and able to work independently without supervision. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to lift 100 lbs. Must be able to lift and carry heavy loads up and down stairs. Must be able to work in all types of weather. Must be able to work well as a team. Salary/Benefits Minimum Pay Rate : $15.00/hour Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html \u00a0 Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Maintenance-Worker-I_R0000840": {"title": "Maintenance Worker I", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Maintenance Worker I Job Description: Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Identifies deficiencies and deviations from maintenance schedules and standards and performs inspection and inspection test of equipment and buildings.\u00a0 Performs general repairs/maintenance as well as minor plumbing and electrical repairs. Assists other mechanical maintenance tradesmen as directed. May operate light or heavy equipment, and maintain equipment and tools. Assists with snow removal as needed. Other job related duties as assigned. Overtime may be required. In order to move to Maintenance Worker II, must have received satisfactory performance evaluations, reached 3 years of experience, and attended all required University trainings. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Ability to read, write and follow directions. Basic knowledge of fundamental mechanical, electrical, plumbing and heating/cooling. 0 - 3 years of experience in specific trade (i.e., plumbing, electrical, etc.) or equivalent education. Must be familiar with and adhere to all the safety rules and regulations for the University Safety Policy which apply to the work environment. Valid Driver\u2019s license. Good hygiene and cleanliness is required at all times Must adhere to the company uniform policy. Maintain a clean vehicle and make office aware of maintenance issues Follow rules and regulations as described in the company Handbook Job Hours: Typical hours are Monday \u2013 Friday 7:00 a.m. - 3:30 p.m. unless otherwise specified. Any schedule may be adjusted as needed and some overnights will be required with inclement weather events, campus events or campus emergencies. Physical Requirements Considerable physical activity. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing, or pulling required of objects up to 50 pounds. Physical work is a primary part (more than 70%) of job. Must be able to lift and carry heavy items up and down stairs. Must be able to spend significant amount of time outside in all weather conditions. Work environment involves exposure to potentially dangerous materials and situations that require following extensive safety precautions and may include the use of protective equipment. Work involves almost constant exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, toxic chemicals, biohazardous materials, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, and/or loud noises. Salary/Benefits Minimum Pay Rate : $15.00/hour Employee Benefits: This is a full-time position with full benefits and annual, holiday and sick leave. The university offers a generous benefits package, including tuition remission for graduate and undergraduate classes at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, retirement program with a match as well as a generous paid time off schedule. For a complete list of employee benefits please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html \u00a0 Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Campus-Safety-Patrol-Officer--Accepting-Applications-_R0001035": {"title": "Campus Safety Patrol Officer (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Campus Safety Patrol Officer (Accepting Applications) Job Description: The Campus Safety Patrol Officer is a key member of the university\u2019s Public Safety team, responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Officers conduct proactive patrols, respond to incidents and emergencies, enforce university policies, and provide exceptional service to the campus community. This role requires professionalism, integrity, and a commitment to community-oriented safety practices. The Campus Safety Patrol Officer reports to the Shift Supervisor / Director of Public Safety. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Patrol campus grounds and buildings via foot or vehicle to ensure safety and security.\u00a0 Conduct routine safety checks of facilities and residence halls, securing access points as needed.\u00a0 Respond promptly to calls for service, alarms, and emergency situations.\u00a0 Provide safety escorts for students, faculty, and staff upon request.\u00a0 Direct traffic and enforce parking regulations in accordance with university policy.\u00a0 Support Shift Supervisors in daily operations and follow directives as assigned.\u00a0 Complete detailed incident reports prior to shift change.\u00a0 Enforce university rules, regulations, and policies with fairness and consistency.\u00a0 May be required to work independently during emergency situations or periods of limited supervision.\u00a0 Foster a welcoming and respectful environment through professional and courteous interactions.\u00a0 Perform other job-related duties as assigned.\u00a0 Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\u00a0 Familiarity with crime prevention strategies, community policing principles, and de-escalation techniques.\u00a0 Understanding of university operations, student development, and campus culture.\u00a0 Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a customer service mindset.\u00a0 Ability to remain calm and effective in high-pressure or emergency situations.\u00a0 Commitment to the mission and values of the university and the Public Safety department.\u00a0 Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: High school diploma or equivalent required.\u00a0 Valid driver\u2019s license with a clean driving record.\u00a0 Must successfully pass a criminal background check.\u00a0 Ability to obtain CPR and basic first aid certification within six months of hire (training provided).\u00a0 Physically capable of performing foot patrols, climbing stairs, and responding to emergencies.\u00a0 Willingness to work rotating shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and special events.\u00a0 Ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment after completion of training.\u00a0 Salary/Hours/Benefits Minimum Pay Rate : $16.50/hour Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Custodial-Worker--Accepting-Applications-_R0001012": {"title": "Custodial Worker (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodial Worker (Accepting Applications) Job Description: Ensuring that the University is neat and safe as well as accomplishing this in a timely manner. Essential Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 Performs routine and comprehensive custodial maintenance of assigned facilities. Vacuums, shampoos and spot cleans carpets and furniture as needed; washes windows. Removes trash in accordance with established procedures. Cleans and disinfects restrooms, locker rooms, and other facilities as specified; stocks facilities with paper and supplies. Reports and responds to emergency calls for custodial assistance. Identifies stains and uses proper chemicals for removal. Maintains inventory and submits written requests for supplies; tests and evaluates new supplies and equipment. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: \u00a0 Experience with stripping and waxing the floors and shampooing carpets may be required Must be familiar with and adhere to all the safety rules and regulations of the College safety policy which apply to the work environment. Ability to read, write and follow instructions. Must be able to work in adverse conditions. Must be able to work under pressure and with short deadlines. Over time on weekends may be required. Must be able to work on feet all day. Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs. \u00a0 Minimum Pay Rate: $15.00/hour \u00a0 Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/HVAC-Preventive-Maintenance-Technician_R0000760": {"title": "HVAC Preventive Maintenance Technician", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: HVAC Preventive Maintenance Technician Job Description: Perform all duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Identifies deficiencies and deviations from maintenance schedules and standards and performs regular Preventive Maintenance on various HVAC equipment. Performs general repairs/maintenance. Assists other HVAC tradesmen as directed. May operate light or heavy equipment, and maintains equipment and tools. Assists with snow removal as needed. Other job-related duties as assigned. Overtime may be required. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: High school diploma or GED. Ability to read, write and follow directions. Basic computer skills. Intermediate to advanced knowledge of mechanical, Low Voltage electrical, heating/cooling and general repairs. Must be familiar with and adhere to all the safety rules and regulations for the University Safety Policy which apply to the work environment. Know how to Lockout/Tagout equipment. Valid driver\u2019s license. Physical Requirements: Considerable physical activity. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing or pulling required objects up to 50 pounds. Physical work is a primary part (more than 70%) of the job. Must be able to lift and carry heavy items up and down stairs. Must be able to spend a significant amount of time outside in all weather conditions. Be able to work off ladders and on roofs. Work environment involves exposure to potentially dangerous materials and situations that require following extensive safety precautions and may include the use of protective equipment. Salary/Benefits Minimum Pay Rate: $24.00/hour \u00a0 Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Director-of-Academics---Student-Athlete-Development_R0001303": {"title": "Director of Academics & Student Athlete Development", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Academics & Student Athlete Development Job Description: The Director of Academics and Student-Athlete Development leads academic support and student-development services for the University\u2019s Division I student-athletes. Reporting directly to the Deputy Director of Athletics, with a dual reporting relationship to the Associate Provost\u2019s Office, the director collaborates with the Center for Student Success and the Executive Director of Advising to monitor academic progress, coordinate support services, promote student-athlete development, and support NCAA academic reporting and compliance. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Monitor and oversee the academic progress of approximately 700 student-athletes participating in 26 Division I sports, and assign teams to the Assistant Director of Academics and Student-Athlete Support and the Graduate Assistant for Student-Athlete Support Services in support of departmental academic goals. Provide direct academic support to assigned varsity sports, including men\u2019s rugby, cheerleading, and dance. Meet individually with assigned student-athletes and facilitate communication between student-athletes and faculty members when appropriate. Coordinate and recommend academic and personal support services for student-athletes, including tutoring, learning services, counseling, and academic support courses. Collaborate with campus departments, including the Career Center, Office of Service, Student Life, and Counseling Services, on student-athlete development initiatives. Use the Sports Tracking Calendar in conjunction with team travel schedules to coordinate class-dismissal notifications and issue team travel letters before each competitive season. Plan and coordinate student-athlete programs and events, including the Student-Athlete Leadership Retreat, Student-Athlete Kickoff, Title IX training, guest speakers, community service activities, and the Emmits Awards Show. Serve as advisor to the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee (SAAC) and collaborate with the Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference on student-athlete initiatives. Assist the Office of Compliance with the collection, validation, and submission of data required for NCAA Academic Progress Rate (APR) and Graduation Success Rate (GSR) reports, as directed by the Director of Compliance and the Deputy Director of Athletics. Perform other duties as assigned. \u00a0\u00a0 Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Knowledge of NCAA rules, regulations, and academic standards applicable to student-athletes. Ability to manage multiple priorities, complete work accurately and on time, and work independently with sound judgment. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across the University. Demonstrated commitment to teamwork, student success, confidentiality, and professional service. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Two to five years of relevant experience in higher education, intercollegiate athletics, academic advising, student support, or a related field preferred. Physical and Scheduling Requirements Ability to work at a computer and communicate with students, faculty, staff, and external partners for extended periods. Ability to move between campus offices and athletic facilities. Ability to work evenings or weekends in support of student-athlete programs, events, and operational needs. Salary/Benefits: $50 ,000 - $55,000/year (Actual compensation will be commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications ). Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Pro-Advisor_R0001304-1": {"title": "Pro Advisor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Pro Advisor Job Description: The Pro Advisor plays a vital role in supporting students\u2019 successful transition to college and career. Working collaboratively with faculty academic advisors, this position provides guidance on university expectations and resources while assisting students in developing personalized academic and personal success plans. The ProAdvisor delivers comprehensive, proactive, and developmentally appropriate support that promotes student growth in academic, personal, and professional areas. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provide Personalized and Effective Transitional Advising \u00a0 Provide holistic, proactive, and comprehensive transitional advising to majors in the assigned College or School. Collaborate with the Dean and faculty advisors of the assigned College or School for the purpose of understanding all majors/programs and supporting faculty advisors. Collaborate with the Dean and faculty advisors in the assigned College or School on matters related to student success and retention specific to each of the majors/programs. Communicate effectively with academic advisors and faculty (within and across the Schools/College) on matters related to student success and retention. Establish effective partnerships with university colleagues to support student success and retention initiatives. Provide proactive, individualized, and major/program-specific support to each student including review of their degree plan and the resources necessary to ensure engagement and success. Serve as a liaison between students and key campus resources, including the Registrar\u2019s Office, Financial Aid, Learning Services, Library, Career Services, Student/Residence Life, and other university services. Monitor student progress by accessing and analyzing key academic data including attendance, mid-term grades, course registration, course withdraws, incompletes, credit recovery, and GPAs. Based on the analysis of key academic data, act on behalf of the student by providing student interventions/referrals as needed and communicating with academic advisors and appropriate faculty. Support students in their academic journey by helping them identify and overcome obstacles to success. Guide students in setting and achieving individual goals while fostering personal accountability. \u00a0 Maintain Student Confidentiality \u00a0 Maintain accurate and confidential records, collect data, and prepare reports related to advising, planning, evaluation, and assessment. Ensure compliance with institutional policies, procedures, and regulations. \u00a0 Participate in Student Intervention, Recruitment, and Orientations Participate in university events related to recruiting, alumni relations, and orientation, including Open Houses, Homecoming, and similar activities. Work occasionally in the evenings and weekends in support of student needs, opportunities, and/or events. \u00a0 Participate in Professional Growth and Responsibilities \u00a0 Engage in professional development opportunities focused on student success and retention. Utilize data to identify critical trends and challenges related to student engagement in the assigned majors. Share trends and challenges with the Dean and Provost. Demonstrate strong interpersonal, cultural competency, and communication skills to engage effectively with students, parents, faculty, and staff. Exhibit excellent organizational, multitasking, and problem-solving abilities. Communicate effectively through both oral and written formats, including group presentations. Thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative work environment, managing fluctuating workloads and meeting deadlines. Provide outstanding customer service to students, families, and the campus community. Utilize Microsoft Office, Canvas, Jenzabar, early alert monitoring tools, and web-based communication platforms. Demonstrate a commitment to the mission of the university. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Required Qualifications \u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in education, counseling, student development, or a related\u00a0 field required. Minimum of two years of experience in academic support, advising, retention, transition programs, or related areas in a higher education setting.\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Skills and Qualities \u00a0 The ideal candidate will demonstrate: A proactive and student-centered approach to advising. Strong analytical and critical-thinking abilities. A passion for student success and engagement. The ability to build meaningful relationships with diverse student populations. Application File Requirements \u00a0 When submitting your application, please include the following: Resume or CV Cover letter Document with contact information for at least three work references \u00a0 Salary/Benefits: This is a full-time, exempt position with a budgeted annual salary range of $45,000 to $48,000 with a bachelor\u2019s degree plus experience, or $50,000 to $55,000 with a master\u2019s degree plus experience. Actual compensation will be commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications. This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Visitor-Experience-Specialist_R0001299": {"title": "Visitor Experience Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Visitor Experience Specialist Job Description: Under the supervision of the Associate Director of Admissions for Events, the Visitor Experience Specialist is responsible for the administration and continuous improvement of the University's campus visit experience. The Visitor Experience Specialist serves as a key member of the Admissions team by analyzing visitor engagement data, implementing communication and service strategies, coordinating campus partnerships, and providing recommendations to enhance the prospective student experience. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Coordinate and oversee the daily campus visit experience for prospective students and families, ensuring a consistent, high-quality visitor experience aligned with enrollment goals. Serve as a primary customer service representative for the Admissions Office front lobby. Supervise front desk student workers and provide support in recruiting, training, scheduling, developing, and recognizing student ambassadors. Manage daily visit calendar in the Admissions CRM (Slate) which includes event reporting, survey evaluations and all event email communication to visitors. Collaborate with faculty, staff, student leaders, and campus partners to ensure effective execution of campus visit experiences. Coordinate communication plans for prospective visitors, including pre-visit, visit-day, and post-visit engagement strategies. Manage the Admissions email account, including responding to inquiries and forwarding communications as appropriate. Monitor and assess visitor satisfaction and engagement data, identifying opportunities for program enhancement and recommending improvements to Admissions leadership. Assist in routine data management, office inventory management, and payment processing. Assist other team members, where applicable, including covering areas or duties not initially assigned. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: A bachelor's degree is required. Two to three years of experience in higher education, student services, admissions, event coordination, customer engagement, or a related field preferred. Strong customer service skills with the ability to interact professionally with students, families, faculty, staff, and external constituents. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Experience leading, training, mentoring, or coordinating student employees, volunteers, or peer leaders preferred. Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and the ability to learn new software applications and systems. Ability to work weekends for major admissions events and programs. Salary Range: $40,000 - $43,000/year (Actual compensation will be commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications) . Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---Engineering-Management--Accepting-Applications-_R0001287": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Management (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Management (Accepting Applications) Job Description: The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University invites applications for part-time Adjunct Faculty in Engineering Management beginning Spring 2027 and ongoing. The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business is accredited by the International Accreditation Council for Business Education (IACBE) and is committed to preparing students for lives of significance in business and society. Our programs emphasize ethics, leadership, entrepreneurship, and global perspectives, consistent with Mount St. Mary\u2019s mission as a Catholic liberal arts university. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach assigned upper-division courses in Engineering Management, including Systems Engineering, Quality Control & Lean Six Sigma, and Engineering Management Capstone. Deliver engaging online instruction and maintain high academic standards. Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. Adhere to course outcomes and assessment standards established by the Bolte School of Business. Apply relevant academic and professional expertise in engineering management, systems engineering, quality control, Lean Six Sigma, project management, operations, or related fields. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Required Master\u2019s degree in Engineering, Engineering Management, Industrial Engineering, Systems Engineering, Operations, or a related field, OR a Ph.D. in one of these areas. Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence. Preferred Prior university-level teaching experience. Professional or industry experience in engineering, engineering management, systems engineering, quality management, Lean Six Sigma, project management, operations, or a related field. Relevant professional certifications, such as Lean Six Sigma, are desirable. Experience applying quantitative and analytical methods to engineering, quality, operations, or process-improvement problems. Evidence of scholarly engagement and professional development. Salary \u00a0 $3500/per course How to Apply \u00a0 Please attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for references. Student teaching evaluations may also be submitted , if available Full Time/Part Time: Part time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Plumber-II_R0001288": {"title": "Plumber II", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Plumber II Job Description: Perform all duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Key duties and responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Install, repair and maintain plumbing systems and components Review building plans and specifications to determine the layout for plumbing and related materials Identify required tools and special equipment Locate and mark positions for connections and fixtures Install supports and hangers for pipe, fixtures and equipment Assemble and install valves and fittings Install, repair and maintain water treatment equipment, piping and controls Install, repair and maintain underground storm sanitary and water piping systems Install, repair and maintain sinks, tubs and toilets, water heaters and conditioners Install, repair and maintain plumbing fixtures, appliances and trim Test pipe systems and fixtures for leaks Maintain all building codes, installation requirements and relevant legislation Perform scheduled maintenance service on plumbing systems and fixtures Apply all codes to installations, repairs and maintenance Ensure all requirements as specified by the manufacturer of systems and fixtures are met Ensure all installations, repairs and maintenance are properly sized, aligned, supported, graded Ensure all installations, repairs and maintenance meet the requirements of the appropriate codes Ensure all installations, repairs and maintenance meet environmental protection requirements Assists with snow removal as need. In order to move to Master Plumber must have received satisfactory performance evaluations, reached 5+ years of experience, acquired all necessary licensing, and attended all required University trainings. Must be willing to train/mentor Plumber I. Must be familiar with and adhere to all the safety rules and regulations for the University\u2019s Safety Policy which apply to the work environment. Must be able to adhere to deadlines and exhibit solid customer service and a strong ability to work well with others. Other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalency. Ability to read, write and follow instructions. Basic, proficient math skills are needed to carry out measurements. 5+ years of experience Valid driver's license required. Overtime may be required. Good hygiene and cleanliness is required at all times Must adhere to the company uniform policy. Maintain a clean vehicle and make office aware of maintenance issues Follow rules and regulations as described in the company Handbook Job Hours: Typical hours are Monday \u2013 Friday 7:00 a.m. - 3:30 p.m. unless otherwise specified. Any schedule may be adjusted as needed and some overnights will be required with inclement weather events, campus events or campus emergencies. Minimum Pay Rate: $22.00/Hour Salary/Benefits This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Athletic-Facilities---Event-Manager_R0001273": {"title": "Athletic Facilities & Event Manager", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Athletic Facilities & Event Manager Job Description: The Athletics Facility and Event Manager serves as a key member of the Athletics Operations & Facilities team and is responsible for supporting the planning, coordination, and execution of athletic events and facility operations for Mount St. Mary\u2019s University. This position assists in creating exceptional game day experiences for student-athletes, coaches, fans, officials, and visiting teams while ensuring safe, efficient, and compliant operation of athletics facilities. This position reports directly to the Director of Athletic Facilities & Operations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Event Management Lead game day operations for athletic events and venues, ensuring successful execution from planning through post-event breakdown for assigned sports. Develop and implement detailed event management plans, timelines, and operational procedures. Coordinate staffing and logistics needs with internal and external partners Ensure competition surfaces and ARCC spaces are safe and properly prepared for internal and external competitions, events, and programs. Serve as a primary point of contact for visiting teams and game officials for assigned events. Coordinate with the Associate Director of Athletics & Recreation for Operations on visiting team logistics, including facility access, practice schedules, locker room assignments, and game day needs. Foster positive relationships with conference partners, NCAA representatives, vendors, and external constituents. Facility Management Assist with the day-to-day operation and stewardship of Athletics facilities. Conduct daily/weekly facility walk-through for assigned sports. Monitor and communicate facility needs and operational concerns at weekly Operations meetings with campus partners. Collaborate with Recreation Facility Supervisor on ARCC facility maintenance, risk management, policies, and procedures. Supervise the ARCC as needed during operational hours and special events. Department Support Assist in preparing fields and facilities for recreational events & competitions. Work collaboratively with Recreation & Wellness on internal and external event logistics. Assist in the creation and maintenance of operational manuals, guidelines, and event information materials. Oversee game day staff for assigned sports. Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of operational policies, procedures, and best practices. Run on- & off-campus errands as needed. Maintain positive and collaborative interoffice relationships Perform other duties as assigned by the Director for Athletic Facilities & Operations. Maintain positive and collaborative interoffice relationships Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Sport Management, Business Administration, Event Management, Recreation, or a related field. One (1) year of experience in athletics operations, event management, facility operations, or a related field. Demonstrated organizational, project management, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a dynamic environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and flexible hours as required by athletic & recreation events and department needs. Knowledge of and compliance with institutional, conference and NCAA rules, both those general in nature and those which apply specifically to their job responsibilities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong attention to detail and commitment to operational excellence. Ability to build collaborative relationships with campus partners and external stakeholders. Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills. Exceptional customer service orientation. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Working Conditions Frequent evenings, weekends, and holiday work. Moderate physical activity, including standing, walking, lifting, and moving event equipment. Ability to work in outdoor environments and varying weather conditions during events Targeted Salary $45,500/year (Actual compensation will be commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications .) This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Director-of-Student-Conduct---Community-Standards_R0001281": {"title": "Director of Student Conduct & Community Standards", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Student Conduct & Community Standards Job Description: Reporting to the Vice President for Student Life, the Director of Student Conduct & Community Standards serves as the University's lead educator and administrator for student conduct and community standards. Through a student-centered and developmental approach, the Director promotes accountability, integrity, personal responsibility, and community well-being while advancing the mission and values of Mount St. Mary's University. The Director provides leadership for the day-to-day operations of the Student Conduct Office and oversees a fair, educational, and inclusive conduct process grounded in student learning, restorative practices, and ethical decision making. As the University's primary hearing officer, the Director is responsible for the administration of the Student Code of Conduct, management of complex conduct cases, and the development and oversight of a campus conduct board adjudication process. Through educational interventions, conflict resolution strategies, developmental conversations, and restorative approaches, the Director helps students understand the impact of their decisions, repair harm when appropriate, and develop the skills necessary to become responsible members of the Mount community and society. Working collaboratively with Residence Life and Housing, Public Safety, Counseling Services, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and other campus partners, the Director identifies behavioral trends, develops proactive educational initiatives, and contributes to student retention, persistence, and success. Leveraging assessment, data-informed decision making, and collaborative partnerships, the Director helps foster a safe, inclusive, and thriving campus community while supporting the holistic growth and development of students. ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES: Student Conduct Administration & Adjudication \u00a0 Provide operational leadership for the Student Conduct Office, including case intake, investigations, hearings, resolutions, and\u00a0follow\u2011up.\u00a0 Manage\u00a0the\u00a0student conduct processes in alignment with institutional policy, including student rights, adjudication procedures, restorative justice practices, and alternative resolution options.\u00a0 Serve as the\u00a0primary hearing officer\u00a0for student conduct cases, including complex,\u00a0high\u2011impact, or sensitive matters.\u00a0 Establish, implement, and oversee a\u00a0student conduct board, including recruitment, training, supervision, and ongoing development of board members.\u00a0 Facilitate the ongoing review, revision, and implementation of the Student Code of Conduct.\u00a0 Collaboration & Community Engagement \u00a0 Partner with Residence Life, Housing, and Public Safety to\u00a0identify\u00a0behavioral trends, develop preventative strategies, and implement coordinated interventions.\u00a0 Collaborate with campus partners to review and respond to reports related to student concerns, safety hazards, and potential violations of university policies. Work together with faculty, staff, and campus partners to implement individual and community-based solutions. Work in partnership with Residence Life and Housing to train Resident Assistants to respond to behavioral concerns, address\u00a0community\u2011level\u00a0issues, accurately document incidents, and support residential student populations.\u00a0 Education, Training, and Leadership \u00a0 Develop and facilitate educational programs focused on community standards, ethical decision-making, conflict resolution, restorative practices, and responsible citizenship. Design and implement learning-focused sanctioning and intervention strategies that support student growth, accountability, and personal development. Support education, training, and change management efforts related to student conduct for campus stakeholders.\u00a0 Assist\u00a0with alcohol and other drug education and prevention initiatives in collaboration with campus partners.\u00a0 Serve as a resource and advocate for students, faculty, and staff navigating student conduct concerns.\u00a0 Maintain a visible presence at campus events and student activities.\u00a0 Represent Student Conduct and Student Life on university committees, working groups, and campus\u00a0initiatives as\u00a0assigned.\u00a0 Assessment, Reporting, and Strategic Initiatives Collect, analyze, and report student conduct data to identify trends, emerging concerns, and opportunities for proactive intervention. Utilize conduct and behavioral data to inform prevention efforts, policy development, and student support strategies. Contribute to student retention and success efforts through data-informed practices, coordinated care strategies, and early intervention initiatives. Develop and maintain assessment measures related to student conduct outcomes, student learning, and community standards education. Prepare annual and semester reports highlighting conduct trends, educational outcomes, sanction effectiveness, and recommendations for continuous improvement. Partner with campus stakeholders to evaluate the effectiveness of conduct processes, educational interventions, and prevention efforts. Collaborate with Student Life leadership to support divisional assessment goals and institutional effectiveness initiatives. Research emerging trends, best practices, and legal developments in student conduct and community standards to support continuous improvement and innovation. Compliance, Technology, and Special Assignments \u00a0 Serve as a Title IX Deputy and participate in\u00a0Title IX processes\u00a0as designated, including hearings, meetings, and investigations.\u00a0 Work closely with Public Safety to ensure compliance with the Clery Act requirements for campus safety initiatives and required training for students, faculty, and staff.\u00a0 Serve as both a Campus Security Authority and Mandatory Reporter. Support the implementation and management of student conduct and student success technology platforms.\u00a0 Perform other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Student Life.\u00a0 JOB REQUIREMENTS: EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, and SKILLS \u00a0 Master\u2019s degree\u00a0required\u00a0in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or a related field.\u00a0 3\u20136 years of progressively responsible professional experience\u00a0in student conduct, residence life, or a closely related area.\u00a0 Demonstrated experience serving as a hearing officer and managing student conduct processes.\u00a0 Knowledge of student development theory, restorative practices, and student conduct best practices.\u00a0 Strong organizational, planning, and communication skills.\u00a0 Ability to build trusting, respectful relationships with students, staff, and campus partners. Familiarity with student conduct and student success technology platforms (e.g., Advocate or similar), preferred.\u00a0 Proficiency\u00a0with Microsoft Office Suite and institutional systems (e.g.,\u00a0Workday\u00a0or similar).\u00a0 Ability to remain calm, professional, and empathetic in\u00a0high\u2011pressure\u00a0or emergencies\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and respond effectively to\u00a0emerging\u00a0concerns.\u00a0 SALARY RANGE & COMPENSATION \u00a0 The salary range for this position is\u00a0 $58,000\u2013$65,000 annually , commensurate\u00a0with education, experience, and qualifications.\u00a0 This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Assistant-Professor-Lecturer-of-Marketing_R0001072": {"title": "Visiting Professor of Marketing", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Visiting Professor of Marketing Job Description: The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University invites applications for a full-time Visiting Professor of Marketing position beginning August 2027. This is a one-year position with the possibility of one- year renewals. We seek to build an inclusive faculty that can engage the interests of our student population. The University has a strong institutional commitment to inclusive excellence in its educational programs and employment practices. We actively seek and welcome applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those with demonstrable commitments to a more inclusive society and world. Successful candidates will share our commitment to the dignity and solidarity of all persons, the value of intercultural understanding, and will be able to articulate how they can contribute to the Mount\u2019s Catholic liberal-arts mission. Additional information about Mount St. Mary\u2019s University is available at www.msmary.edu. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The teaching requirement for this 10-month contract is 24 credits (8 classes) between the Fall and Spring semesters and will include a combination of undergraduate and graduate courses in marketing. Undergraduate courses are primarily delivered in person and offered during the day with some evening options, while graduate courses are delivered using on-line synchronous and asynchronous formats. The successful candidate will also serve as the primary contact for student recruitment and advising for the marketing concentration and minor. It is likely that the required teaching load will involve 5-6 different course preparations. All faculty are expected to serve the Mount by advising students majoring in the school's programs, developing course curriculum, participating in assessment, remaining current in their discipline, and performing other duties as assigned. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Qualifications Required: Ph.D. or Graduate degree in Marketing or a related discipline. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence. Preferred: Professional or industry experience in the field. Prior university-level teaching experience. Evidence of scholarly engagement and professional development. Salary Range: The salary ranges below represent budgeted hiring averages and are provided for transparency. Final salary offers are competitive and determined based on discipline-specific market factors, qualifications, experience, and rank. In some cases, salaries may fall outside the listed averages. $70,000 \u2013 $80,000, depending on rank assigned. Employee Benefits: Mount St. Mary's University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support employees and their families. Benefits include generous sick leave, comprehensive health insurance coverage, and an employer-sponsored retirement plan with a University contribution. Employees also have access to tuition remission opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate coursework. Eligible dependents may benefit from undergraduate tuition remission as well as participation in tuition exchange programs, which provide opportunities to pursue studies at hundreds of participating colleges and universities nationwide. Additional benefits include flexible spending accounts, wellness resources, employee assistance programs, and a variety of campus community perks that contribute to a rewarding and supportive work environment. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html About the Bolte School of Business The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business is accredited by the International Accreditation Council for Business Education (IACBE) and is committed to preparing students for lives of significance in business and society. Our programs emphasize ethics, leadership, entrepreneurship, and global perspectives, consistent with Mount St. Mary\u2019s mission as a Catholic liberal arts university. Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Assistant-Professor-Lecturer-of-Finance_R0001073": {"title": "Visiting Professor of Finance", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Visiting Professor of Finance Job Description: The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University invites applications for a full-time Visiting Professor position beginning August 2027. This is a one-year position with the possibility of one-year renewals. We seek to build an inclusive faculty that can engage the interests of our student population. The University has a strong institutional commitment to inclusive excellence in its educational programs and employment practices. We actively seek and welcome applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those with demonstrable commitments to a more inclusive society and world. Successful candidates will share our commitment to the dignity and solidarity of all persons, the value of intercultural understanding, and will be able to articulate how they can contribute to the Mount\u2019s Catholic liberal-arts mission. Additional information about Mount St. Mary\u2019s University is available at www.msmary.edu. Essential Duties and Responsibilities:\u00a0 The teaching requirement for this 10-month contract is 24 credits (8 classes) between the Fall and Spring semesters and will include a combination of undergraduate and graduate courses in finance. Undergraduate courses are primarily delivered in person and offered during the day with some evening options, while graduate courses are delivered using on-line synchronous and asynchronous formats. The successful candidate will also serve as the primary contact for student recruitment and advising for the finance major and minor. It is likely that the required teaching load will involve 5-6 different course preparations. All faculty are expected to serve the Mount by advising students majoring in the school's programs, developing course curriculum, participating in assessment, remaining current in their discipline, and performing other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Required: Ph.D. or Graduate degree in Finance Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States Prior university-level teaching experience. Preferred: Professional or industry experience in the field. Evidence of scholarly engagement and professional development. An earned Professional Certification (e.g. CFP, CFA, or ChFC) Salary Range: The salary range below represents the anticipated salary range for this position and is provided for transparency. Final salary offers are determined based on qualifications, experience, and discipline-specific market factors. $70,000 \u2013 $80,000, depending on qualifications, background and experience. Employee Benefits: Mount St. Mary's University offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support employees and their families. Benefits include generous sick leave, comprehensive health insurance coverage, and an employer-sponsored retirement plan with a University contribution. Employees also have access to tuition remission opportunities for both undergraduate and graduate coursework. Eligible dependents may benefit from undergraduate tuition remission as well as participation in tuition exchange programs, which provide opportunities to pursue studies at hundreds of participating colleges and universities nationwide. Additional benefits include flexible spending accounts, wellness resources, employee assistance programs, and a variety of campus community perks that contribute to a rewarding and supportive work environment. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html About the Bolte School of Business The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business is accredited by the International Accreditation Council for Business Education (IACBE) and is committed to preparing students for lives of significance in business and society. Our programs emphasize ethics, leadership, entrepreneurship, and global perspectives, consistent with Mount St. Mary\u2019s mission as a Catholic liberal arts university. Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Assistant-Athletic-Trainer--Women-s-Rugby---Women-s-Water-Polo-_R0001274": {"title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer-(Women's Rugby & Women's Water Polo)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Athletic Trainer-(Women's Rugby & Women's Water Polo) Job Description: The Sports Medicine Department at Mount St. Mary's University is looking for a certified athletic trainer to work with our nationally ranked women\u2019s rugby team and women's water polo team. The Assistant Athletic Trainer will provide quality, comprehensive care for student-athletes through prevention, evaluation, care, and the treatment of injuries and illnesses and assist with injury rehabilitation. This includes the screening and referral of student-athletes to team physicians when appropriate. This role will serve as a staff athletic trainer including practice/game coverage and team travel. The Assistant Athletic Trainer will be responsible for compiling and maintaining injury and treatment documentation for the Sports Medicine Department, assisting with the supervision and daily operation of the athletic training facilities and assisting with the establishment, coordination, supervision, and monitoring athletic training services for all student-athletes. Mount St. Mary\u2019s University seeks a candidate who can communicate with coaches and athletic department staff on a variety of issues, including but not limited to the Sports Medicine Department policies and procedures, student-athlete status, activity restrictions, and treatment/rehabilitation, appointment compliance and progress. This role will assist the staff in the upkeep of facilities, emergency equipment and modalities. Collaboration with other departments \u2013 Academic Services, Mental Health, Nutrition, Strength and Conditioning, and the Equipment Room are key in providing comprehensive healthcare and a positive experience for the student-athlete. The Assistant Athletic Trainer will report directly to the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. This position as an Assistant Athletic Trainer is a 12-month salaried position with a complete benefits package. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Some of the major responsibilities include: Serve as the staff athletic trainer for the women\u2019s rugby and women's water polo teams; with the potential of sport, practice and game coverage of other teams as assigned by the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. Provide quality and comprehensive care for ALL student-athletes through prevention, evaluation, care and treatment of injuries and illnesses and assist with injury rehabilitation. Travel with assigned teams. Compile and maintain injury and treatment documentation for the Sports Medicine Department including injury tracking and reporting. Assist with the supervision of the electronic medical records. Assist with establishing, coordinating, supervising, and monitoring of athletic training services to ALL student-athletes. Other duties as assigned by the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Master\u2019s degree in a health-related field is preferred (Athletic Training, Sports Medicine, etc.) Board of Certification Athletic Trainer (new grads welcome to apply; experience preferred) Current Maryland State Athletic Training Licensure or eligible for. Knowledge of\u00a0NCAA\u00a0rules and regulations. Ability to work nights and weekends, travel involved. CPR and First AID certified. Strong interpersonal communication, and organizational skills. Training in bloodborne pathogens. Soft Tissue Mobilization certification (preferred). Targeted Salary $50,000/year (Actual compensation will be commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications ). Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Registered-Behavior-Technician--RBT---Accepting-Applications-_R0001075": {"title": "Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-27\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) (Accepting Applications) Job Description: At the Blue Peak Center for ABA at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, we are dedicated to improving the lives of individuals with autism through evidence-based treatment methodologies. Our brand-new center will feature both one-on-one and group settings under the careful guidance of highly qualified supervisors. Our team is passionate about making a positive impact and providing compassionate, high-quality care. In addition to the support we provide our clients, we aim to provide a unique experience for those working within the center with a strong focus on training, mentorship, and clinician wellbeing. If you are enthusiastic, compassionate, and are looking to make a difference for children with autism, we invite you to apply for the Registered Behavior Technician (RBT) position. RBTs provide direct therapy, under the supervision of a Board Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA), to develop a child\u2019s communication, social-emotional, and adaptive daily living skills. RBTs will engage in structured teaching sessions, collect data, and collaborate with the BCBA to identify the best course of treatment for the clients they work with. This position is fulltime and will work out of the Blue Peak Center for Applied Behavior Analysis at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University. The Center is located in Emmitsburg, MD. Mount St. Mary\u2019s University is an equal opportunity employer with a strong institutional commitment to inclusive excellence in its educational programs and employment practices. We actively seek and welcome applications from candidates with exceptional qualifications, particularly those with demonstrable commitments to a more inclusive society and world. Successful candidates will share our commitment to the dignity and solidarity of all persons, the value of intercultural understanding, and will be able to articulate how they can contribute to the Mount\u2019s Catholic mission. Additional information about Mount St. Mary\u2019s University is available at www.msmary.edu. Responsibilities Acquire and maintain RBT certification Implement written treatment plans as developed by the BCBA Build and maintain positive relationships with clients Work in 1:1 or small group settings with clients Collect data related to client goals to inform treatment decisions Submit regular written reports of client progress Collaborate with supervisors, coworkers, clients, and stakeholders effectively and professionally Qualifications Must have at least a high school diploma and be at least 18-years-old. Some higher education in psychology, education, human services, or related field preferred, but not required. Experience working with children Experience with individuals with development disabilities and/or behavior challenges preferred Effective oral and written communication skills Reliable transportation to and from our Emmitsburg center Pass a criminal background check from state and federal registries Active RBT certification preferred or ability to obtain RBT certification within 45-60 days of hire. Salary & Benefits: $19-23 per hour, depending on experience Opportunities for professional development Opportunities for career growth Full time hours; consistent schedule Paid training Health insurance, including dental and vision Educational Benefits Limited tuition remission for graduate and undergraduate programs ( that are flexible around your work schedule ) Tuition exchange and undergraduate tuition remission for dependents after 2 years of employment This is a full-time position with full benefits and annual, holiday and sick leave. The university offers a generous benefits package, including a limited tuition remission package for graduate and undergraduate classes at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, retirement program with a match as well as a generous paid time off schedule. For a complete list of employee benefits please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Position Requirements: Work Under Pressure: The candidate must be able to effectively manage high-stress situations. Must demonstrate the ability to work with tight deadlines while maintaining productivity and quality of work. \u00a0 Physical Agility: The candidate must be capable of standing and remaining active for the majority of the workday. Ability to work on feet for extended periods (e.g., 8-hour shifts or longer). The candidate must be able to run or move quickly as needed during the course of the workday, often in response to time-sensitive tasks or emergencies. Lifting Requirements: The candidate must be able to lift and carry objects weighing up to 40 lbs. on a regular basis. Must practice proper lifting techniques to ensure safety and avoid injury. Schedule Monday \u2013 Friday, 8-hour shift. Hours of operation: 7:30 AM \u2013 4:30 PM Staff hours will be either 7:30 \u2013 4:00 PM or 8:00 \u2013 4:30 PM consistent daily and communicated in advance. Work Location At our center in Emmitsburg, MD. 2 miles from Mount St. Mary\u2019s University towards downtown Emmitsburg. At least 3 professional references must be provided with application. Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Campus-Events-Logistics-Worker--Accepting-Applications-_R0001013": {"title": "Campus Events/Logistics Worker (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Campus Events/Logistics Worker (Accepting Applications) Job Description: Perform all duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: \u00a0 Duties include, but are not limited to: Event set-ups/breakdowns, including tents, stages, floor covering, barricades, tables, chairs etc.\u00a0 Office moves, including furniture, file cabinets, etc., ensuring that appropriate moving procedures are followed to prevent damage. Dormitory moves including beds/bunking beds, desks, chests, etc. \u00a0 May be asked to assist any other department within the campus community and will be required to perform any other duties as assigned by immediate Supervisor/Manager/Director. Must be willing and able to work independently without supervision. Job Requirements: High school diploma or GED.\u00a0 Must attain on-site training within 30 days of hire or have proof of previous training in event set-up/ packing/wrapping/moving/loading of furniture and safety training on proper lifting. A uniform, issued by MSMU will be required.\u00a0 Job Hours Hours will vary depending upon University events but will typically range between 6:30 a.m. - 8:00 p.m. with varying weekly schedules.\u00a0 Overtime during weekdays, weekends and holidays will be required as needed. A weekend rotation schedule will be implemented depending upon staffing, workloads and University events.\u00a0 Any schedule may be adjusted as needed and some overnights will be required with inclement weather, university events or campus emergencies. \u200b Physical Requirements Must be able to lift a minimum of 50 lbs. Must be able to lift and carry heavy loads up and down stairs. Must be able to work in all types of weather. Must be able to work well as a team. Salary/Benefits Minimum Pay Rate: $15.00/hour \u00a0 Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Nursing-Clinical-Director_R0001152": {"title": "Nursing Clinical Director", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Nursing Clinical Director Job Description: Under the direction of the Director for the School of Nursing, the Clinical Director of Nursing provides leadership and oversight for the clinical education component of the School of Nursing at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University. This position is responsible for coordinating high-quality clinical learning experiences, supporting clinical faculty and preceptors, ensuring compliance with clinical and regulatory requirements, and promoting student readiness for professional nursing practice. In keeping with the School of Nursing\u2019s mission, the Clinical Director also helps ensure that clinical education forms students in ethical clinical judgment, respect for human dignity, and compassionate, person-centered care especially in service to communities most in need. Main Position Duties Ensure clinical placements, simulation, and skills experiences reinforce the School of Nursing\u2019s mission to form ethical, compassionate, and clinically proficient nurses guided by the principles of Catholic Social Teaching. Identify and collaborate with clinical partners and community agencies to prioritize learning experiences that support care for vulnerable populations. Coordinate and oversee clinical education experiences across all nursing courses, including clinical placements, skills labs, and simulation. Develop, maintain, and evaluate clinical partnerships with healthcare agencies and community organizations. Develop orientation resources for clinical faculty and preceptors that clarify program expectations for person-centered care, professionalism, and formation in ethical clinical judgment. Ensure clinical experiences meet program outcomes, accreditation standards, and Maryland Board of Nursing requirements. Collaborate with the Director and Associate Director of Nursing to align clinical education with curriculum goals and student learning outcomes. Recruit, orient, support, and evaluate clinical faculty and preceptors in collaboration with program leadership. Monitor student clinical performance and support remediation or intervention plans as needed. Maintain documentation related to clinical compliance, including affiliation agreements, preceptor qualifications, and student requirements. Participate in accreditation, assessment, and reporting activities related to clinical education. Teach clinical and/or didactic nursing courses as assigned based on program needs and qualifications. Integrate structured reflection and debrief practices within clinical education to strengthen students\u2019 reflective mindset and readiness for compassionate practice. Required Qualifications Graduate degree in nursing from an accredited program. Eligibility for Registered Nurse licensure in the State of Maryland. Minimum of two years of clinical nursing experience. Experience in clinical instruction, clinical coordination, or nursing education. Strong organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills. Demonstrated commitment to supporting and advancing the Catholic mission and identity of Mount St. Mary\u2019s University through one\u2019s professional responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree in nursing (Ph.D. or DNP). Experience coordinating clinical placements or managing clinical partnerships. Familiarity with accreditation and regulatory expectations related to nursing clinical education. Demonstrated ability to lead clinical education in a mission-driven context, including formation of students and preceptors, respect for human dignity, and person-centered care. Hours: 40-hour week (Weekends are occasional) Targeted Salary: $82,500/year (Actual compensation will be commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications) . Employee Benefits: This full-time position includes a comprehensive benefits package, featuring annual, holiday, and sick leave. The University offers a generous suite of benefits, including tuition remission for both graduate and undergraduate courses at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University, an employer-sponsored retirement contribution, and a robust paid time off program. For a complete list of employee benefits, please visit: https://inside.msmary.edu/more/human-resources/index.html Full Time/Part Time: Full time"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---Business-School--Accepting-Applications-_R0001000": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - School of Business (Accepting Applications)", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-15\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct Faculty - School of Business (Accepting Applications) Job Description: The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business at Mount St. Mary\u2019s University invites applications for part-time Adjunct Faculty for various business positions beginning Spring 2026 and ongoing. The Richard J. Bolte, Sr. School of Business is accredited by the International Accreditation Council for Business Education (IACBE) and is committed to preparing students for lives of significance in business and society. Our programs emphasize ethics, leadership, entrepreneurship, and global perspectives, consistent with Mount St. Mary\u2019s mission as a Catholic liberal arts university. Essential Duties and Responsibilities \u00a0 Teach assigned courses in Accounting, Finance, Management, or Marketing. \u00a0 Deliver engaging instruction and maintain high academic standards. \u00a0 Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. \u00a0 Adhere to course outcomes and assessment standards established by the Bolte School of Business. \u00a0 \u200b Job Requirements: Education, Experience and Skills: Required \u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in Accounting , Finance, Management, or Marketing (or a related field), OR a Ph.D. in one of these areas. \u00a0 Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence. \u00a0 Preferred \u00a0 Prior university-level teaching experience. \u00a0 Professional or industry experience in the field. \u00a0 Evidence of scholarly engagement and professional development. \u00a0 Salary \u00a0 Compensation is commensurate with qualifications and experience . \u00a0 How to Apply \u00a0 Please attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for references. Student teaching evaluations may also be submitted , if available. \u00a0 Full Time/Part Time: Part time"}}, "rows": {"https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Grounds-Worker--Accepting-Applications-_R0001298": {"school_id": 599, "posting_url": "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Grounds-Worker--Accepting-Applications-_R0001298", "job_title_in_post": "Grounds Worker (Accepting Applications)", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-06"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Maintenance-Worker-I_R0000840": {"school_id": 599, "posting_url": "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Maintenance-Worker-I_R0000840", "job_title_in_post": "Maintenance Worker I", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-06"}, "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Campus-Safety-Patrol-Officer--Accepting-Applications-_R0001035": {"school_id": 599, "posting_url": "https://msmu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MSMU/job/Emmitsburg-Campus/Campus-Safety-Patrol-Officer--Accepting-Applications-_R0001035", "job_title_in_post": "Campus Safety Patrol Officer (Accepting Applications)", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_s